XUI's `-nofix_dts` for the 4.0 bucket (FFmpeg 4.4.x).

The panel runs live restreams with `-copyts ... -nofix_dts` on the 4.0 binary.
XUI's 2018 build (N-92517-gd0f5942-XUI10FFMPEG) added a `fix_dts` bool (default 1)
that gates fftools' write_packet() DTS fixup, and dropped libavformat's
monotonic / pts>=dts rejection. Stock ffmpeg has neither: on a backward DTS step
in the source it clamps every packet to last_dts+1 until the source catches up,
so hundreds of frames land in a few ms — the panel reads 200+ fps, audio and
video drift apart, audio drops out. With this patch `-nofix_dts` passes the
source timestamps through untouched, as XUI did; without it nothing changes
(fix_dts on → fftools keeps DTS monotonic, so the dropped lavf checks never fired).

diff -ru a/fftools/ffmpeg.c b/fftools/ffmpeg.c
--- a/fftools/ffmpeg.c
+++ b/fftools/ffmpeg.c
@@ -810,7 +810,7 @@
 
     av_packet_rescale_ts(pkt, ost->mux_timebase, ost->st->time_base);
 
-    if (!(s->oformat->flags & AVFMT_NOTIMESTAMPS)) {
+    if (fix_dts && !(s->oformat->flags & AVFMT_NOTIMESTAMPS)) {
         if (pkt->dts != AV_NOPTS_VALUE &&
             pkt->pts != AV_NOPTS_VALUE &&
             pkt->dts > pkt->pts) {
